 "title": "Say or Clap",
 "diff": "Medium",
 "src": "Flipkart Data Engineer OA (IIT BHU, handwritten)",
 "body": "<p><code>N</code> players numbered 1 to N sit in a circle and count upwards: the first player says 1, the next says 2, and so on, going round the circle. For each number the correct action is:</p><ul><li><strong>Clap</strong> (<code>C</code>) if the number is divisible by 3 or contains the digit 3;</li><li>otherwise <strong>Say</strong> it (<code>S</code>).</li></ul><p>You are given a string of <code>S</code> and <code>C</code>: its i-th character is the action performed for number i. The first player to perform a wrong action is eliminated. The game then restarts with the remaining players, in increasing order of their numbers: counting starts again from 1 with the lowest-numbered player, and the string is read again from its first character.</p><p>This repeats until one player remains, or until the whole string is read without a mistake. Print the elimination order and the players still in the game.</p><p class='muted'>Reconstructed from a handwritten report. The rule for a string with no mistakes was filled in for this mock.</p><h3>Function to complete</h3><p>Complete <code>sayOrClap(n, actions)</code>. It returns two rows: the eliminated players in order (or just -1 if nobody is eliminated), then the remaining players in increasing order.</p><p class=\"muted\">Input reading and printing are handled for you, like on LeetCode. The input format below is what the tests and <i>Custom input</i> use.</p>",
 "inp": "Line 1: <code>N</code>. Line 2: the action string.",
 "out": "Line 1: the eliminated players in order, separated by spaces, or <code>-1</code> if nobody is eliminated. Line 2: the remaining players in increasing order.",
 "cons": [
